    </div>

    <div role="tabpanel" id="panel-ai" aria-labelledby="tab-ai" class="panel" hidden>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="how small muted">
          This tab sets the two kinds of recommender side by side. <strong>Humans</strong> are the doctor, nurse, remote doctor,
          therapist, personal trainer and layperson (six). <strong>AI</strong> is AI in general, an AI diagnostic tool, an AI chatbot and an
          AI fitness coach (four). A doctor using AI is a person plus a tool, so it is shown on its own. Each person’s score for a
          group is the average of their ratings of its recommenders. The doctor-versus-AI comparison in the dissertation (H6, H7, E)
          is one pair; this is the exploratory version across all of them. It was not preregistered.
        </p>
      </div>

      <section class="section" id="hva-gap" aria-labelledby="hva-gap-title">
        <h2 id="hva-gap-title">The gap</h2>
        <p class="intro">
          People rated humans higher than AI on all three things. On average, trust was {f1(hv[0].diff)} points higher for humans
          (d = {f2(hv[0].d)}), intuition {f1(hv[2].diff)} points higher (d = {f2(hv[2].d)}), and perceived quantitative reasoning
          {f1(hv[1].diff)} points higher (d = {f2(hv[1].d)}), the smallest of the three.
        </p>
        <StatTable
          id="table-hva"
          title="Table 15. Humans versus AI, paired by person"
          columns={hvCols}
          rows={hvRows}
          note={`Paired t tests on each person’s average rating. Only people who rated every recommender in both groups are included (${Math.min(...hva.tests.map((t: any) => t.human_vs_ai.n))} to ${Math.max(...hva.tests.map((t: any) => t.human_vs_ai.n))} of ${full.sample.n}). d is the mean difference over the SD of the differences.`}
        />

        <h3 class="fig-title" id="fig-hva-clouds">Figure 9. Every person, humans against AI</h3>
        <p class="intro">
          Each outline is how people’s averages are spread, each dot is one person, and the diamond is the group average with its
          bootstrapped 95% interval. The doctor using AI sits between the two groups on all three.
        </p>
        {
          hvCloud.map((c: any) => (
            <div class="cloud">
              <h4 class="mini">{c.measure}</h4>
              <Raincloud rows={c.rows} grid={hva.densityGrid10} domain={[0, 10]} tickStep={1} xJitter={0.2} xLabel={`${c.measure}, average rating (0 to 10)`} ariaLabel={`${c.measure}: each person's average for human recommenders, a doctor using AI, and AI recommenders`} />
            </div>
          ))
        }

        <h3 class="fig-title" id="fig-hva-dir">Figure 10. How many people show the gap?</h3>
        <p class="intro">
          The averages hide the people who go the other way. Counting each person’s own difference: {hvDir[0].higher} of
          {' '}{hvDir[0].higher + hvDir[0].same + hvDir[0].lower} rated humans higher on trust, {hvDir[0].lower} rated AI higher, and
          {' '}{hvDir[0].same} rated them equal.
        </p>
        <DirectionBars rows={hvDir} />

        <details class="more">
          <summary>If a doctor using AI is counted differently</summary>
          <StatTable
            id="table-hva-alt"
            title="Table 16. Other ways to draw the line"
            columns={hvAltCols}
            rows={hvAltRows}
            note="The same paired tests with the doctor using AI shown on its own, compared with each group, or counted as AI as the notebook does. The conclusion does not change."
          />
